/*
    Saturation, ADAA (antiderivative anti-aliasing, first order) : the output for the input "u" of the shape is the mean of the
    shape between the previous input u0 and u, (F(u) - F(u0)) / (u - u0) ; close inputs : the shape of their middle ; u0 and
    F(u0) are kept in s[11], s[12] (the states of the channel) ; "fr" : F(u0) is valid (the shape has not changed), else it
    is computed again ; the output is half a sample late and, where the shape is linear, filtered as the mean of two
