/*
    Mode Grains : grains drawn at random in the loop (it moves, as in mode Brage), created at random times, "density" per
    second on average : periodic, random (a Poisson process : exponential intervals) or between both (its_Rdr_GrRand).
    A grain : a length (its_Rdr_GrSize ms), a plateau
    (its_Rdr_GrPlat % of the length), a fade-in (its_Rdr_GrFade % of the rest, the fade-out : the rest), a gain
    (its_Rdr_GrVol dB), a rate (the speed of the reader, its absolute value, modulated) and a direction (forward with the
    probability (1 + its_Rdr_GrDir) / 2), each one with its random factor (its_Gr_Rnd) ; one channel of the line, chosen at
    random among the channels read, to an output channel chosen at random among those of the reader (it may have more
    output channels than the line has channels) ; the whole grain in the loop (its_Br_Pick). Its envelope : the curve
    its_Rdr_GrCurve (its table, see its_Crv_Build), its rise stretched over the fade-in, the level of its plateau, its fall
    stretched over the fade-out ; without a curve (or a waveform), linear ramps ; the envelope times the gain, at most 1.
    At most its_RdGr_Max grains at once ; their state in the work area of the reader (its_RdGr_WkSz words).
*/

// a random factor for the setting "a" [1 ... 5] : drawn in [1, a], or its inverse (one time out of two) ; a = 1 : 1
function its_Gr_Rnd(a) local(x)
(
    a = max(1, min(5, a));
    (a <= 1) ? 1 : ( x = 1 + rand(1) * (a - 1); (rand(1) < 0.5) ? x : 1 / x; );
);

// a new grain of the reader "reader" (mode Grains, @sample) in its work area "wk", for its line "lcbl" and its speed "v"
// (modulated) ; nothing if all the places are taken
function its_Gr_New(reader, wk, lcbl, v)
local (g, i, n, pl, fi, rho, st, ra, rb, nc, no, k)
(
    g = wk + its_RdW_Hdr; i = 0;
    while ((i < its_RdGr_Max) && (g[its_Gr_N] > 0)) ( g += its_RdGr_Sz; i += 1; );
    (i < its_RdGr_Max) ? (
        n = max(4, floor(max(10, min(10000, reader[its_Rdr_GrSize])) * its_Gr_Rnd(reader[its_Rdr_GrSizeR]) * srate / 1000));
        pl = floor(n * min(100, max(0, min(100, reader[its_Rdr_GrPlat])) * its_Gr_Rnd(reader[its_Rdr_GrPlatR])) / 100);
        fi = floor((n - pl) * min(100, max(0, min(100, reader[its_Rdr_GrFade])) * its_Gr_Rnd(reader[its_Rdr_GrFadeR])) / 100);
        rho = max(0.01, min(SPDMAX, abs(v) * its_Gr_Rnd(reader[its_Rdr_GrSpdR]))) * reader[its_Rdr_AdjInc];
        (rand(1) >= 0.5 * (1 + max(-1, min(1, reader[its_Rdr_GrDir])))) ? (rho = -rho);
        st = reader[its_Rdr_Start];
        ra = st + floor(reader[its_Rdr_LowPosSec] * srate); rb = st + floor(reader[its_Rdr_HighPosSec] * srate);
        nc = max(1, min(reader[its_Rdr_BfChanUsed], lcbl[its_Lin_ChCnt] - reader[its_Rdr_Bf1stChan])); // (channels read)
        no = max(1, reader[its_Rdr_OutW]); // (output channels)
        g[its_Gr_J] = 0;
        g[its_Gr_Pos] = its_Br_Pick(ra, rb, n * abs(rho), rho) - its_Rd_OffDisp(reader); // (the input Offset : back)
