    irregularity of the intervals ; at each tick a new value : the common one with the probability "corr" (the common clock
    draws it), else its own draw (the law is kept : a Binary stays +-1) ; Step : held ; Smooth : from the previous value to
    the new one over the interval (smoothstep) ; Walk : a step of "walk" times a draw, reflected within [-1, 1] (the common
    step with the probability "corr") ; then the steps (n levels within [-1, 1]), the glide (one pole)
    the trigger (its source, times its gain) : at a rising edge above the threshold, a tick, and the clock starts again ;
    clock Common : the first channel of the trigger (the common clock) ; clock Own : the channel c of the trigger for the
    channel c (and its first channel for the common clock : the common value) ; rate 0 : the triggers only
    the slots of a channel (and of the common clock) : 0 the phase of the clock, 1 the inverse of the length of its interval
    (relative to the rate), 2 the value at the start of the interval, 3 the new value, 4 the value (before the steps ; the
    common clock : the step of the mode Walk), 5 the value after the glide, 6 the value of the mode Walk, 7 the samples
